BUNDLED DATA
- Offline place list (apps/web/src/data/gazetteer.json): GeoNames cities1000 extract,
  https://www.geonames.org/ , CC BY 4.0, as packaged by all-the-cities (MIT).
- Star catalogue and constellation figures (packages/sky/src/data/stars.json): d3-celestial
  by Olaf Frohn, BSD-3-Clause (packages/sky/src/data/D3-CELESTIAL-LICENSE); stars from the
  Hipparcos catalogue.
- World outline for the eclipse map (packages/sky/src/data/land.json): Natural Earth
  1:110m land, public domain, as packaged by world-atlas (ISC).

ONLINE SERVICES
- Place search: Open-Meteo Geocoding API, https://open-meteo.com/ , free for non-commercial
  use under 10,000 calls a day, CC BY 4.0, built on GeoNames data (https://www.geonames.org/,
  CC BY 4.0). If this project ever carries ads or subscriptions, it needs a paid Open-Meteo plan.
  The public OpenStreetMap Nominatim service is deliberately not used on the website:
  its usage policy forbids client-side autocomplete.

ARTWORK AND TEXT
The planet renders, wheel, medallions, backgrounds and 3D models are generated by the
scripts in blender/ and are covered by the project license, as are the interpretation texts in
packages/interpretations, which were written for this project. The painted starry backgrounds
are decorative and do not show real star positions; the 3D view's "Real stars" mode does.
